## Secrets — generated Swift is derived from these, never commit them
# Anything in Config/ starting with `.env` (.env, .env.MyApp, .envrc …)
/Config/.env*
# …or ending in `.env` (secrets.env, prod.env …)
/Config/*.env
# Exception: the committed template. Must come after the rules above —
# gitignore applies the last matching pattern.
!/Config/.env.example

## Generated sources — any folder named `Generated`, at any depth.
# No leading slash, trailing slash = directories only. Git does not descend
# into an excluded directory, so nothing inside can be re-included later.
# The [Gg] class keeps the rule case-consistent: gitignore matching is
# case-sensitive on Linux CI, while macOS git usually sets core.ignorecase=true,
# so a bare `Generated/` could be ignored locally yet committed by a runner.
[Gg]enerated/

## macOS
.DS_Store

## XcodeGen — the project is generated from project.yml, never committed.
# Run `xcodegen generate` after cloning and in CI before xcodebuild.
# Schemes live in project.yml, and SPM versions are pinned exactly there too,
# so nothing inside the bundle needs keeping — including Package.resolved,
# which is why the whole bundle can be excluded outright. Trailing slash =
# directories only; no leading slash, so nested projects match at any depth.
*.xcodeproj/

## Xcode
build/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
*.moved-aside
*.hmap
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM
timeline.xctimeline
# Archives: default to ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/Archives, but CI often passes
# -archivePath into the working tree. Trailing slash — .xcarchive is a bundle.
*.xcarchive/

## Credentials — plaintext, and unrecoverable once in history
# Used by SwiftPM for authenticated package repos and binary artifacts, and by
# curl/git. Normally ~/.netrc, but copies land in repos for CI.
.netrc
# Defence in depth against accidentally leaking credential files and signing
# keys — none of these belong in a repo, so ignoring them costs nothing.
# (.cer is deliberately absent: pinned certificates are public keys.)
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.certSigningRequest

## Swift Package Manager
.build/
.swiftpm/
# Package.resolved is not committed: dependency versions are pinned exactly in
# project.yml. Consequence for CI — do NOT pass -disableAutomaticPackageResolution
# or -onlyUsePackageVersionsFromResolvedFile to xcodebuild; both fail without a
# resolved file present.
Package.resolved

## fastlane
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots/**/*.png
fastlane/test_output